p=Path('jos-cct/brief.html');s=p.read_text().replace('<h2>Five-minute demonstration script</h2>','''<h2>Connected native-service demonstration</h2><p><a href="/registration/jos-cct">Open the staff walkthrough</a> or <a href="./?view=connected">view the public evidence snapshot</a>. Three fictional cases are persisted in the sandbox: JOS-NATIVE-001 has completed native approval, local-bank credit and statement reconciliation; JOS-NATIVE-003 is waiting in AWE review; JOS-NATIVE-002 is untouched for a new walkthrough.</p><p>The native flow uses the existing custom registry adapter, PBMS eligibility and entitlement workers, Approval Workflow Engine, signed SPAR mapping, Bridge, local Example Bank and native statement processing. A fixed NGN 25,000 is used solely as a simulator test amount; no USD conversion is implied. Native attendance is synthetic evidence gated by the Jos adapter, not a school-system connection or the production base/top-up rule.</p><p>For the minister, first inspect the completed sample and its source identifiers, then open the pending AWE case. Use the untouched sample to demonstrate registration synchronisation, eligibility, enrolment and calculation. Refresh native status between asynchronous steps. Staff actions are audited; native AWE uses the sandbox integration administrator. Do not claim production separation of duties.</p><h2>Browser-only planning demonstration script</h2>''').replace('Session actions are simulated and reversible. They do not write to the registry, PBMS or a bank.','Actions in the browser-only planning mode are simulated and reversible. The separate connected staff mode writes genuine fictional records to the sandbox services and local Example Bank ledger; it cannot use the configured live payment rails because none are connected to this route.');p.write_text(s)
